---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import LoopVideo from '../components/LoopVideo.astro';
import OfferIcon from '../components/OfferIcon.astro';
import PageTitle from '../components/PageTitle.astro';
import '../styles/tutoring.css';
---

<BaseLayout title="Tutoring With Me — Trapp Tutoring">
	<section class="tutoring-hero">
		<div class="tutoring-hero-media">
			<LoopVideo src="videos/erin-teaching-30s.mp4" objectPosition="center bottom" />
		</div>
		<PageTitle id="about" text="About me" />
		<div class="tutoring-hero-copy">
			<p>
				Hi, I'm Erin Trapp! I am a K-12 teacher, and I completed my BA in Teaching English as a
				Second Language at Winona State University. My specialties are Dyslexia, Literacy, ESL,
				Spanish, and Early Childhood Development. I have a wide range of teaching experiences,
				including 1st grade, 7th grade literacy, high school Spanish and ESL, Pre-K, as well as
				six years of one-on-one virtual tutoring.
			</p>
			<p>
				During the beginning years of my teaching career, I observed students at various levels
				struggle with literacy. I was struck by the lack of adequate support for students with
				Dyslexia in the traditional educational system, and I wanted to become a part of the
				solution. I dove into studying the challenges that students with Dyslexia face and
				discovered the importance of learning an Orton-Gillingham based approach. In speaking
				with a Barton tutor with 15+ years of experience, who later became my mentor, I was
				inspired by the structure and proven effectiveness of the Barton Reading &amp; Spelling
				System. Combining my years of experience in one-on-one tutoring and my passion for
				literacy, I became a Barton-trained, full-time tutor. The ability to read opens up a
				world of opportunities, and it is such rewarding work to empower students with this
				skill.
			</p>
			<p>
				Many students who struggle with reading have had very difficult, humiliating, and
				demoralizing experiences in traditional educational settings. It is no surprise that
				they would have some hesitation about starting tutoring for reading and spelling!
				During my online sessions, I strive to make the student feel safe, comfortable,
				encouraged, and challenged. My passion is empowering students to master skills that
				they thought were inaccessible to them and have fun while doing it!
			</p>
		</div>
	</section>

	<section class="tutoring-clip">
		<LoopVideo src="videos/student-gameplay-from-1m28.mp4" />
	</section>

	<section class="tutoring-facts" aria-labelledby="tutoring-facts-heading">
		<h2 id="tutoring-facts-heading">What is learning with Trapp Tutoring like?</h2>
		<ul class="tutoring-fact-list">
			<li class="tutoring-fact">
				<details>
					<summary>
						<OfferIcon name="one-on-one" />
						<h3>One-On-One</h3>
						<span class="tutoring-fact-mark" aria-hidden="true"></span>
					</summary>
					<div class="tutoring-fact-body">
						<p>
							The Barton Reading &amp; Spelling System is designed for consistent, one-on-one
							instruction to see the best results and ensure that each student receives the
							needed support.
						</p>
					</div>
				</details>
			</li>
			<li class="tutoring-fact">
				<details>
					<summary>
						<OfferIcon name="remote" />
						<h3>Fully Remote</h3>
						<span class="tutoring-fact-mark" aria-hidden="true"></span>
					</summary>
					<div class="tutoring-fact-body">
						<p>
							I teach entirely online so I can meet with students no matter where they live. My
							schedule is flexible to meet the needs of your busy life!
						</p>
					</div>
				</details>
			</li>
			<li class="tutoring-fact">
				<details>
					<summary>
						<OfferIcon name="interactive" />
						<h3>Interactive and Multisensory</h3>
						<span class="tutoring-fact-mark" aria-hidden="true"></span>
					</summary>
					<div class="tutoring-fact-body">
						<p>
							I use <a href="https://www.teachwithkoala.com/">Koala Go</a> as my teaching
							platform because it provides a highly interactive remote teaching option. Koala Go
							allows me to teach the same content in a gamified, engaging way! You do not need
							an account; I will simply send you a link to my classroom.
						</p>
					</div>
				</details>
			</li>
			<li class="tutoring-fact">
				<details>
					<summary>
						<OfferIcon name="barton" />
						<h3>Barton System</h3>
						<span class="tutoring-fact-mark" aria-hidden="true"></span>
					</summary>
					<div class="tutoring-fact-body">
						<p>
							The Barton Reading &amp; Spelling System is intentionally structured for crucial
							building blocks of reading and spelling to be learned in an effective sequence. It
							is an Orton-Gillingham based intervention for reading and spelling, comprised of
							10 levels. It takes most students about two to three years to complete all ten
							levels, and the pace depends on the student.
						</p>
					</div>
				</details>
			</li>
			<li class="tutoring-fact">
				<details>
					<summary>
						<OfferIcon name="weekly" />
						<h3>Multiple Times per Week</h3>
						<span class="tutoring-fact-mark" aria-hidden="true"></span>
					</summary>
					<div class="tutoring-fact-body">
						<p>
							To see the best results, it is important to have tutoring 2-3 times each week so
							that the learned skills are not forgotten, but rather can be built upon to see
							impressive improvement. Classes are typically 50 minutes, but modifications can be
							made based on the needs of the student.
						</p>
					</div>
				</details>
			</li>
			<li class="tutoring-fact">
				<details>
					<summary>
						<OfferIcon name="fun" />
						<h3>Fun</h3>
						<span class="tutoring-fact-mark" aria-hidden="true"></span>
					</summary>
					<div class="tutoring-fact-body">
						<p>
							Many of my students start class thinking reading is too challenging for them,
							feeling defeated before the first day. I flip the script and make sure every
							class is accessible, enjoyable, and personalized with tailored games and content
							to the students' interests. I love seeing my students go from discouraged to
							delighted in just 50 minutes!
						</p>
					</div>
				</details>
			</li>
		</ul>
	</section>

	<section class="tutoring-tech" aria-labelledby="tutoring-tech-heading">
		<h2 id="tutoring-tech-heading">What do you need to start tutoring?</h2>
		<ul class="tutoring-tech-list">
			<li>
				<h3>Reliable Internet</h3>
				<p>
					For Koala Go to be supported, you need a download and upload speed of at least 30
					Mbps download / 5 Mbps upload.
					<a class="phrase-link" href="https://www.speedtest.net/">Check your speed on Speedtest</a>.
				</p>
			</li>
			<li>
				<h3>Computer, Chromebook, or iPad</h3>
				<p>
					Koala Go is compatible with all computers, Chromebooks, and iPads. At this time,
					tutoring is not possible via iPhone.
				</p>
			</li>
			<li>
				<h3>Webcam</h3>
				<p>If your computer has a built-in webcam, that will work just fine!</p>
			</li>
			<li>
				<h3>Headset with mouthpiece (preferred)</h3>
				<p>
					Both the student and I will be working with important sound distinctions, so a headset
					helps to ensure that everyone is understood clearly and the sounds are learned
					correctly.
				</p>
			</li>
			<li>
				<h3>Computer mouse (preferred)</h3>
				<p>
					Because my tutoring style is highly interactive, students will be manipulating objects
					on the screen a lot. A mouse may facilitate manipulation, especially for younger kids.
				</p>
			</li>
		</ul>
	</section>

	<section class="tutoring-who" aria-labelledby="tutoring-who-heading">
		<h2 id="tutoring-who-heading">Who is this for?</h2>
		<p>
			Trapp Tutoring is created for any student who is struggling with reading and writing. No
			official diagnosis of Dyslexia is required. In order to successfully use the Barton system,
			the student must:
		</p>
		<ul class="tutoring-who-list">
			<li>be at least 5 years old or in kindergarten.</li>
			<li>speak and comprehend spoken English.</li>
			<li>pass a short student screening that I will administer before we begin tutoring.</li>
		</ul>
	</section>
</BaseLayout>
